    <string name="titan_confirm_activate_title">Activate Titan?</string>
    <string name="titan_confirm_activate_body">Titan first runs the passive privilege check, then asks for Superuser access once. There is no silent escalation: without your confirmation Titan stays at Level 1.</string>
    <string name="titan_confirm_activate_consequence">Possible effect: the Superuser dialog (Magisk, KernelSU or APatch) appears on the TV and can be cancelled.</string>
    <string name="titan_confirm_activate_confirm">Start activation</string>
    <string name="titan_confirm_freeze_title">Freeze app?</string>
    <string name="titan_confirm_freeze_body">The app is disabled for user 0 and force-stopped. Its data stays on the device, but it stays disabled until the system settings re-enable it. This alpha has no restore button in the UI.</string>
    <string name="titan_confirm_isolate_title">Isolate network?</string>
    <string name="titan_confirm_isolate_body">Outgoing traffic of the UID is dropped with an iptables rule. Other apps and streaming stay untouched. This alpha has no release button in the UI.</string>
